[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186096744 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-6b244d67-f2e6-5997-9db2-2abb0586d4be" "question-8875866b-8dd0-5b03-ad00-243a32baa5f0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186097236 :question/problem "Consider the following geometric sequence:\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=-\\frac{2}{3}{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=5,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$\n\nDetermine whether the sequence is convergent or divergent. If it converges, find the limit." :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nThe given sequence is a geometric sequence with the common ratio \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}=-\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nSince $|r|=\\frac{2}{3}<1$, the sequence converges to $0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186095340 :answer-field/correct 17592186095344 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-6b244d67-f2e6-5997-9db2-2abb0586d4be" :question/id #uuid "6b244d67-f2e6-5997-9db2-2abb0586d4be" :question/math-academy-id "q-123333" :question/problem "Consider the following geometric sequence:\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=2{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=-4,\\,n\\ge 1\n$$\n\nDetermine whether the sequence is convergent or divergent. If it converges, find the limit." :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nThe given sequence is a geometric sequence with the common ratio \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}=2.\n$$\n\nSince $|r|=2>1$, the sequence diverges." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4eef3b91-cbf1-5165-b4b4-6db1ea5e763f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4eef3b91-cbf1-5165-b4b4-6db1ea5e763f" :answer-field/id #uuid "4eef3b91-cbf1-5165-b4b4-6db1ea5e763f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-a6fb9534-7b00-51a6-9b6b-3e0661951505" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f4d729f2-8517-5f08-b3f8-1bda0315fedc" "answer-6cdc885e-37b4-5a68-a0b9-c54691be5651" "answer-43955b41-f6e8-5349-9111-56dd4e7126c8" "answer-ba63283c-6ba0-5b52-bd92-e677158a64ba" "answer-a6fb9534-7b00-51a6-9b6b-3e0661951505"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4d729f2-8517-5f08-b3f8-1bda0315fedc" :answer/id #uuid "f4d729f2-8517-5f08-b3f8-1bda0315fedc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Converges to $-4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6cdc885e-37b4-5a68-a0b9-c54691be5651" :answer/id #uuid "6cdc885e-37b4-5a68-a0b9-c54691be5651" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Converges to $0$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-43955b41-f6e8-5349-9111-56dd4e7126c8" :answer/id #uuid "43955b41-f6e8-5349-9111-56dd4e7126c8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Converges to $2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ba63283c-6ba0-5b52-bd92-e677158a64ba" :answer/id #uuid "ba63283c-6ba0-5b52-bd92-e677158a64ba" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Converges to $\\frac{1}{2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a6fb9534-7b00-51a6-9b6b-3e0661951505" :answer/id #uuid "a6fb9534-7b00-51a6-9b6b-3e0661951505" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The sequence diverges" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8875866b-8dd0-5b03-ad00-243a32baa5f0" :question/id #uuid "8875866b-8dd0-5b03-ad00-243a32baa5f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-123334" :question/problem "Consider the following geometric sequence:\n\n$$\n{a}_{n+1}=4{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{4},\\,n\\ge 1\n$$\n\nDetermine whether the sequence is convergent or divergent. If it converges, find the limit." :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a geometric sequence with the first term ${a}_{1}$ and common ratio $r.$ Then, we have the following convergence properties:\n\n- if $|r|<1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to $0$\n\n- if $|r|>1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nMoreover, we have the following edge cases:\n\n- if $r=1,$ the sequence is convergent and converges to ${a}_{1}$\n\n- if $r=-1,$ the sequence is divergent\n\nThe given sequence is a geometric sequence with the common ratio \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{{a}_{n+1}}{{a}_{n}}=4.\n$$\n\nSince $|r|=4>1$, the sequence diverges." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-77095092-5c7c-58b9-9d24-8f2368d8a83f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-77095092-5c7c-58b9-9d24-8f2368d8a83f" :answer-field/id #uuid "77095092-5c7c-58b9-9d24-8f2368d8a83f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-e0c72dcf-0cfe-526c-b0ed-899e73f67e02" :answer-field/choices ["answer-55d44151-35f1-54c2-9d4d-cb890968345b" "answer-f0d2babb-cf96-5a12-b155-7886cd64321e" "answer-0d1a1119-11c9-535c-a456-e45cc9d7de82" "answer-c9f1522c-e116-5be3-a536-f1ce7ed8e514" "answer-e0c72dcf-0cfe-526c-b0ed-899e73f67e02"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-55d44151-35f1-54c2-9d4d-cb890968345b" :answer/id #uuid "55d44151-35f1-54c2-9d4d-cb890968345b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Converges to $-1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f0d2babb-cf96-5a12-b155-7886cd64321e" :answer/id #uuid "f0d2babb-cf96-5a12-b155-7886cd64321e" :answer/type :answer.typ